// `@compileFor` drop is literal: a gated-out decl's symbol never exists, so a reference from KEPT
// code to a dropped decl is a normal unresolved-symbol error — the user must gate both sides (or
// provide a same-named fallback for the complementary flag, as tests/compilefor_mode.kama does).
// Here `onlyRelease` exists only under RELEASE, but the ungated `main` calls it; the default (debug)
// build drops `onlyRelease` and the call dangles.
@compileFor(RELEASE) fn int32 onlyRelease() { return 1; }

fn int32 main() { return onlyRelease(); }
